## Context

PR [#37](https://github.com/wazootech/wazoo-api/pull/37) added `@/lib/worlds-client.ts` with a `worldsAdminClient` helper and `worldsApiErrorDetail` extractor. The account-deletion route in `src/routes/users.ts` still uses raw fetch calls and should be migrated to the generated client.

## Review comment

[r3818212434](https://github.com/wazootech/wazoo-api/pull/37/changes#r3818212434) on `src/routes/users.ts:11` suggests:

```typescript
import { db, id, now } from "@/lib/db";
import { isAdmin, requireScope, respond } from "@/lib/http";
import { UserSchema } from "../lib/schemas";
import { deleteNamespaceWorlds } from "@worlds/client";
import { worldsAdminClient } from "@/lib/worlds-client";
```

## Scope

Replace the hand-rolled `fetch` calls in the account-deletion handler with `worldsAdminClient(env).worlds.deleteNamespace(...)` (or the equivalent `deleteNamespaceWorlds` call), using `worldsApiErrorDetail` for error extraction. Also align the import style with the `@/` path alias convention per [workspace#24](https://github.com/wazootech/workspace/issues/24).

## Blocked on

PR [#37](https://github.com/wazootech/wazoo-api/pull/37) merge (provides the `worldsAdminClient` helper).

## Bug

Exact-match seeks on **xsd:string literals return 0 bindings** even when the quad exists in the store. `FILTER(CONTAINS(...))`/scan-style matches work — only the equality seek path is broken.

**Empirical repro (wazoo-memorybench, LibsqlStore over a smoke DB):**
- `SELECT ?name WHERE { ?p <http://schema.org/name> ?name . FILTER(?name = "Caroline") }` → 5 bindings
- `SELECT ?p WHERE { ?p <http://schema.org/name> "Caroline" }` → **0 bindings**

The second is the seek path — and it's what LLM agents write naturally (exact name matches), so they silently burn steps rediscovering that CONTAINS/LCASE is required. Observed: ~10 of 15 SPARQL tool calls in one recollection run wasted on exact-name queries that all returned empty.

## Root cause — write/read `o_datatype` asymmetry

**Write** (`src/libsql/commit-patch-to-libsql.ts:238`): stores the literal's datatype IRI verbatim:

```ts
o_datatype: object.datatype,   // "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string" for xsd:string
```

**Read-scan** (`src/libsql/quad-store/libsql-quad-query-builder.ts:75`) already knows the write format and normalizes:

```sql
... AND o_type = 'Literal' AND (o_datatype IS NULL OR o_datatype = '' OR o_datatype = 'http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string' OR o_lang IS NOT NULL AND o_lang != '')
```

**Read-seek** (`src/libsql/quad-store/libsql-quad-query-builder.ts:245-254`, `appendTermCondition`) does **not** — for xsd:string *or* rdf:langString it emits `o_datatype IS NULL`, which can never match the stored full IRI:

```ts
if (datatypeValue === xsdStringIri || datatypeValue === rdfLangStringIri) {
  conditions.push(`o_datatype IS NULL`);
} else {
  conditions.push(`o_datatype = ?`);
  args.push(datatypeValue);
}
```

So the seek and the scan disagree on what a "plain string" looks like in `o_datatype`. Same-store impact on both Comunica and the Wazoo SPARQL engine (the seek SQL is shared).

## Suggested fix (mirror the scan path in the seek)

```ts
if (datatypeValue === xsdStringIri) {
  conditions.push(`(o_datatype IS NULL OR o_datatype = '' OR o_datatype = '${xsdStringIri}')`);
} else if (datatypeValue === rdfLangStringIri) {
  conditions.push(`(o_datatype IS NULL OR o_datatype = '' OR o_datatype = '${rdfLangStringIri}')`);
} else {
  conditions.push(`o_datatype = ?`);
  args.push(datatypeValue);
}
```

Plus a test: store a quad with an `"x"^^xsd:string` object and assert the equality seek returns it (mirror the cases already in `libsql-quad-query-builder.test.ts`).

Note: `rdfLangStringIri` and `xsdStringIri` are already defined at the top of `libsql-quad-query-builder.ts`.
